# Sweep trigger marker (Round 3, Task B3)

The presence of this file in a commit pushed to
`review/bench-workspace-ffi` triggers the "Sweep Dispatch (manual)"
workflow (see .github/workflows/sweep-dispatch.yml) — the reduced
concurrency sweep (BTV_SWEEP_TARGET_WALL_SECS=10, 3 modes) on a
GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest runner, as the second REAL execution
environment for the E2 multi-hardware evidence.

Why a marker: workflow_dispatch API calls 404 while this workflow file
exists only on a non-default branch (GitHub registers dispatchable
workflows from the default branch). The push path filter on this file
provides an equivalent manual trigger that works on feature branches.

After the workflow lands on the default branch, prefer workflow_dispatch
and remove the push trigger from the workflow file (this marker then
becomes inert documentation).
